-- title:
--   Hasse root is a Kummer generator of exponent p-1
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime, let $M$ be a non-zero natural number with $5 \le M$ and $p \nmid M$, and let $k$ be an algebraically closed field of characteristic $p$. Let $w$ be an integral weight-one form on $\Gamma_1(M)$ over $k$ in the sense of [`ModularCurve.IntegralWeightOneForm`](def/ModularCurve_IgusaFunctionFieldX1.html#L16), that is: a modular form `w.form` of weight $1$ for $\Gamma_1(M)$ (viewed inside $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{R})$), together with a power series `w.series` over $\mathbb{Z}$ whose image under $\mathbb{Z} \to \mathbb{C}$ is the $q$-expansion of `w.form`, and subject to the requirement that the Laurent series $\mathrm{intSeriesC}\,k\,(w.\mathrm{series})$ over $k$, obtained by reducing `w.series` along $\mathbb{Z} \to k$ and regarding it in $k((q))$, is non-zero. Put $a = w.\mathrm{hasseRootFn} = (\mathrm{intSeriesC}\,k\,(w.\mathrm{series}))^{-1} \in k((q))$. The conclusion is that $a$ is a Kummer generator of exponent $p-1$ over $\mathrm{x1FunctionFieldC}\,k\,M$, the intermediate field of $k((q))$ over $k$ generated by the family `intFormRatiosC k (Gamma1 M)`; unfolded, this asserts the three statements $0 < p - 1$ (truncated subtraction of naturals), $a \ne 0$, and $a^{p-1} \in \mathrm{x1FunctionFieldC}\,k\,M$.
--
--   This is the Kummer-theoretic input for the Igusa tower over $X_1(M)$ in characteristic $p$: it exhibits the inverse reduced $q$-expansion as a radical generator, so that adjoining it to the function field $k(X_1(M))$ gives a Kummer extension of exponent dividing $p-1$, hence a finite separable one. It is used in the construction of the Igusa covering data and in the separability and transcendence statements for the Igusa function field of $X_1(M)$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_isKummerGenerator_hasseRootFn_x1FunctionFieldC.lean

